.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt RENUXINSTALLER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm renuxinstaller
.Nd install Renux to a disk by cloning the running live system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op disk
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility installs Renux onto a disk by cloning the running live system.
It detects the available disks, lets the user select a target (like
.Xr bsdinstall 8 ) ,
partitions it (GPT with a freebsd-boot stage, an EFI System Partition and a
UFS root), formats the partitions, copies the live world to the disk,
installs the boot code and loader (BIOS and UEFI) and writes a proper
.Pa /etc/fstab
and
.Pa /boot/loader.conf .
.Pp
No distribution sets are required: the installer copies the running live
environment.
.Pp
If a
.Ar disk
argument is given, that disk is used without prompting.  Otherwise a list
of detected disks is presented for selection.
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
All data on the target disk is destroyed.
.It
The disk used to boot the live media is refused.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BSDINSTALL_CHROOT"
.It Va BSDINSTALL_CHROOT
Mount point used for the target root.  Defaults to
.Pa /mnt .
.It Va ESP_SIZE
Size of the EFI System Partition.  Defaults to
.Ql 128m .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/boot/loader"
.It Pa /boot/loader
EFI boot loader copied to the target ESP.
.It Pa /etc/motd
Welcome banner shipped to the target.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bsdinstall 8 ,
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in Renux 0.1.
